# Backend Linear Sync

Whenever making a meaningful backend change:

- Find the relevant issue in the AUX Linear team before or during the work.
- After implementation and verification, update that issue with:
  - a concise summary of the behavior changed;
  - the affected backend area;
  - the commit or pull request link when available;
  - tests, type-checks, and builds that were run;
  - remaining work or blockers.
- Keep the issue status aligned with the actual state of the implementation.
- Group trivial follow-up edits into the same update instead of creating noise.
- Never include secrets, credentials, tokens, or private environment values.
- If no suitable issue exists, ask before creating one.
- If Linear is unavailable, tell the user that the update is pending rather than
  silently skipping it.
